// 2. TOOLTIPS
//=====================================================================================================================
t1 = "Reverses the orientation of labels and calculations in the Gann Box, offering alternative analytical perspectives."
t2 = "Extend the drawing of Gann lines or boxes into the future beyond the current last bar to anticipate potential support or resistance levels. This setting is crucial for traders looking to forecast future price movements and prepare for potential market reactions at these extended levels."
t3 = "Enables or disables the display of the Gann Box (price levels, time levels and their backgrounds). The Gann Box is a fundamental tool in Gann analysis, providing insights into potential support and resistance levels, and enabling traders to identify strategic entry and exit points."
t4 = "When enabled, the backgrounds use the single up / down color (up = price rising from low to high, down = price falling from high to low) instead of each level's own color."
t5 = "Enables or disables the display of Gann Curves. When enabled, it draws curves based on Gann percentages to predict potential market movements. These curves offer a dynamic view of potential support and resistance levels as they adjust to changing market conditions, aiding in the analysis of momentum and trend strength."
t6 = "Enables or disables the display of Gann Angles. These are diagonal lines that extend from significant price points to provide insights into future support and resistance levels. Gann Angles are a cornerstone of Gann theory, offering a unique perspective on price and time dynamics that can signal significant market movements."
t7 = "Enables or disables the Gann Fan. The 1/1 line is the box diagonal; every other line is that slope multiplied by its ratio (1/8 is shallow, 8/1 is steep). Lines stop where they reach the edge of the box."
t8 = "When enabled, all fan lines and the background use the single up / down color (up = price rising from low to high, down = price falling from high to low) instead of each line's own color."
t9 = "When enabled, all curves, labels and the background use the single up / down color (up = price rising from low to high, down = price falling from high to low) instead of each curve's own color."
t10 = "How the Gann Box is anchored.\nVisible Window = highest high / lowest low of the bars currently visible on the chart.\nLast Pivots = the most recent confirmed pivot high and pivot low (see Pivot Lookback).\nManual Range = highest high / lowest low between Manual Range Start and Manual Range End (typed in below, exchange timezone)."
t11 = "Bars to the left and right used to confirm a pivot. Only used when Box Anchor is 'Last Pivots'."
t12 = "Start of the range (typed date and time, exchange timezone). Only used when Box Anchor is 'Manual Range'."
t13 = "End of the range (typed date and time, exchange timezone). Only used when Box Anchor is 'Manual Range'."
t14 = "Manual Anchor Time (Day / Month / Year / Hour / Min). Only used when Anchor Type is 'Manual'. The anchor is placed on the first bar at or after this date and time (exchange timezone)."

